{:edb/db-before-t 2551 :edb/db-after-t 2552 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535864 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:18:29.366Z" 13194139535864 true] [17592186147339 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371140 13194139535864 true] [17592186147340 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371128 13194139535864 true] [17592186147340 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371135 13194139535864 true] [17592186147340 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371147 13194139535864 true] [17592186147960 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535864 true] [17592186147960 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe rate at which guests check into a particular hotel one evening is given by the function\n\n$r(t) = 3t^{2} + 2$,\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in guests per hour and $t > 0$ is the time in hours since $6p.m$.\n\nGuests are also checking out of the hotel at a steady rate of $1$ guest per hour.\n\nIf there were $200$ guests in the hotel at $6p.m$, how many guests will there be in the hotel at $9p.m$?" 13194139535864 false] [17592186147960 1100 "The rate at which guests check into a particular hotel one evening is given by the function\n\n$$\nr(t)=3{t}^{2}+2,\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in guests per hour and $t>0$ is the time in hours since $\\text{6}\\,\\text{p.m}.$\n\nGuests are also checking out of the hotel at a steady rate of $1$ guest per hour.\n\nIf there were $200$ guests in the hotel at $6\\,\\text{p.m},$ how many guests will there be in the hotel at $9\\,\\text{p.m?}$" 13194139535864 true] [17592186147960 1145 "Guests are entering the hotel at a rate of $3{t}^{2}+2$ guests per hour and are leaving at a rate of $1$ guest per hour. Therefore, the **rate of change** in the number of guests (call it $R(t)$) is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(t) & =r(t)-1 \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+2-1 \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the **total number of guests** after $t$ hours (call it $T(t)$), we apply the second fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =T(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}R(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =200+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo ensure that $T$ is a function of $t$ only, we use a different variable ($x$) for the integration. \n\nTo find out the number of guests after $3$ hours ($9\\,\\text{p.m}$), we substitute $t=3$ into the above, and evaluate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3) & =200+{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =200+{[{x}^{3}+x]|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =200+[(27+3)-(0)] \\\\  & =200+30 \\\\  & =230\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371128 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371129 13194139535864 true] [17592186371128 1089 "q-140822" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371128 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535864 true] [17592186371128 1100 "Scientists are observing a colony of bugs. The population $P(t)$ of the colony is given by the function\n\n$$\nP(t)=27+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ is the number of bugs, and $t>0$ is the time (in days) since the observation started. \n\nAt what time is the population of the colony a minimum, and what is the number of bugs at this time?" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371128 1113 #uuid "3cbfc231-381e-525d-b699-91d7448dd5be" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371128 1145 "To find when the population is a minimum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(27+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(27)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0$ for $t>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 3({t}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =4 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=2.$\nTo find the number of bugs when $t=2,$ we figure out $P(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2) & =27+{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =27+[{x}^{3}-12x]{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =27+[(8-24)-(0)] \\\\  & =27-16 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $11<27$, we conclude that the minimum population is $11$ bugs, and this happens after $2$ days." 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371130 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371131 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371132 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371133 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371134 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1041 "selection" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371134 13194139535864 true] [17592186371129 1110 #uuid "8f32f3a9-05bc-5d33-9b3d-1012aeff8edd" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371130 1034 "The minimum is $8$ bugs after $4$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371130 1111 #uuid "f365a0e7-5ded-59d2-a249-e16ad446034c" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371131 1034 "The minimum is $27$ bugs after $5$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371131 1111 #uuid "cdb8e3db-3d74-5fdb-8c33-de5ab3a65029" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371132 1034 "The minimum is $15$ bugs after $4$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371132 1111 #uuid "748ef904-c60f-55c3-a6d1-df12163edfc0" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371133 1034 "The minimum is $16$ bugs after $2$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371133 1111 #uuid "cdbe05ee-0a81-554a-8526-4fde84017671" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371134 1034 "The minimum is $11$ bugs after $2$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371134 1111 #uuid "b7e4250f-a608-5da7-a34a-d66c5a4de826" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371135 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371136 13194139535864 true] [17592186371135 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371138 13194139535864 true] [17592186371135 1089 "q-350001" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371135 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535864 true] [17592186371135 1100 "The value $P(t)$ of a painting is given by the function\n\n$$\nP(t)=250+{\\int }_{0}^{t}({3}^{x/4}-27)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ is measured in dollars, and $t>0$ is the time (in years) since the painting was created. \n\nAt what time is the value a minimum, and how much does the painting cost at this time, rounded to the nearest dollar?\n\nThe minimum value is\n$$$\n{{field-1}}\nafter\n{{field-2}}\nyears." 13194139535864 true] [17592186371135 1113 #uuid "11fe5804-48ea-5b4e-be85-64cdc6bfb0cb" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371135 1145 "To find when the value is minimized, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(250+{\\int }_{0}^{t}({3}^{x/4}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(250)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}({3}^{x/4}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}({3}^{x/4}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={3}^{t/4}-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{t/4}-27 & =0 \\\\ {3}^{t/4} & ={3}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{t}{4} & =3 \\\\ t & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=12.$ To find out the value of the painting when $t=12,$ we figure out $P(12):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(12) & =250+{\\int }_{0}^{12}({3}^{x/4}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =250+{[\\frac{4\\cdot {3}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-27x]|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =250+[(\\frac{4\\cdot 27}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-324)-(\\frac{4\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})] \\\\  & =250-324+\\frac{108-4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-74+\\frac{104}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & ≈21,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nSince $21<250,$ we conclude that the minimum value is $$\\,21$, and this happens after $12$ years." 13194139535864 true] [17592186371136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371137 13194139535864 true] [17592186371136 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535864 true] [17592186371136 1041 "field-1" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371136 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371137 13194139535864 true] [17592186371136 1110 #uuid "703015e8-5b93-55e9-9b8e-c639d545c1bb" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371137 1034 "21" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535864 true] [17592186371137 1111 #uuid "d35d8965-743a-59e0-8e76-a4aa86bb5645" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371139 13194139535864 true] [17592186371138 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535864 true] [17592186371138 1041 "field-2" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371138 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371139 13194139535864 true] [17592186371138 1110 #uuid "4c5c5060-9a15-54da-92fe-3bb9e3ff3e35" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371139 1034 "12" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535864 true] [17592186371139 1111 #uuid "3ae0c9b8-ddbd-5e52-9ed8-975eab86b8ff" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371140 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371141 13194139535864 true] [17592186371140 1089 "q-62816" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371140 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535864 true] [17592186371140 1100 "A pipe is filling water into a tank. The rate $r(t)$ at which water enters the tank is given by the function \n\n$$\nr(t)=\\frac{15}{1+7{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in liters per minute, and $t>0$ is the time in minutes since the pipe started running. Initially, there were $60$ liters of water in the tank.\n\nWhich integral gives the quantity of water in the tank $t$ minutes after the inlet started running?" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371140 1113 #uuid "e2a03aa4-3991-5f7a-acb2-a9c864ceae09" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371140 1145 "We're given the **rate of change** of volume $r(t).$ To find the total volume $V(t)$ after $t$ minutes, we apply the second fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(t) & =V(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =60+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo ensure that our final function is a function of $t$ only, we use a different variable ($x$) for the integration." 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371142 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371143 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371144 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371145 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371146 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1041 "selection" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371143 13194139535864 true] [17592186371141 1110 #uuid "6b0e360e-f754-518e-83d0-36d71887ffae" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371142 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{60}(60+\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535864 true] [17592186371142 1111 #uuid "b91681f5-dafd-5ae5-9480-1bba9ac64a35" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371143 1034 "60+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535864 true] [17592186371143 1111 #uuid "069fee2b-0ab2-5523-b9f4-f00d80af40cf" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371144 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{60}\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535864 true] [17592186371144 1111 #uuid "c68ab4de-3335-548e-9862-25a53602e52a" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371145 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535864 true] [17592186371145 1111 #uuid "79acb368-c7d4-5c6a-a58c-2564e378a0fb" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371146 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{t}(60+\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535864 true] [17592186371146 1111 #uuid "47fe281a-6efd-5b5e-8c5c-8c997beac1bd" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371147 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371148 13194139535864 true] [17592186371147 1089 "q-62834" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371147 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535864 true] [17592186371147 1100 "The total number of participants $S(t)$ registered for an online conference after $t$ days is given by the function\n\n$$\nS(t)=40+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in days, since the conference was announced. \n\nAt what time is the number of participants at a minimum, and how many participants are registered at this time?" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371147 1113 #uuid "4ac669a1-558e-5ec3-b564-f595f3a2738c" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371147 1145 "To find when the number participants is minimized, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(40+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(40)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4t-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=0$:\n\n$$\n4x-16=0\\,⟹\\,t=4\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=4.$ To find out how many participants are registered when $t=4,$ we figure out $S(4)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(4) & =40+{\\int }_{0}^{4}(4x-16)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =40+{[2{x}^{2}-16x]|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =40+[(2(4)^{2}-16(4))-(0)] \\\\  & =40-32 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $8<40$, we conclude that the minimum number of participants is $8$, and this occurs after $4$ days." 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371149 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371150 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371151 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371152 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371153 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1041 "selection" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371152 13194139535864 true] [17592186371148 1110 #uuid "3d306fef-d854-55dc-ba90-b04ca9fc0cd4" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371149 1034 "The minimum is $32$ participants  after $4$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371149 1111 #uuid "b4a1fdd9-69b3-5a41-b7a0-52260184e6c1" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371150 1034 "The minimum is $32$ participants  after $0$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371150 1111 #uuid "8788b6b3-d86e-54c7-839b-a26a9cd34b73" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371151 1034 "The minimum is $40$ participants  after $4$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371151 1111 #uuid "f860378e-aff9-5453-9825-32863e89a7f9" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371152 1034 "The minimum is $8$ participants  after $4$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371152 1111 #uuid "752b5fe1-f46b-5016-aded-d1e0bde22b3f" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371153 1034 "The minimum is $40$ participants  after $0$ days" 13194139535864 true] [17592186371153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535864 true] [17592186371153 1111 #uuid "971d9a84-1d2e-5757-9dcf-8c6fa4c2bcdf" 13194139535864 true